{"type":"text","timestamp":1794543372794,"sessionID":"ses_e2ce4c822ffeajVHIjUYYvzhCo","part":{"id":"prt_1d31eba19002HxlzfrpSqp4THt","sessionID":"ses_e2ce4c822ffeajVHIjUYYvzhCo","messageID":"msg_1d31ea1b70015wUhl9XWPkWdoZ","type":"text","text":"T004 is complete. Both files are edited and all three gates pass.\n\n**Files written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts` — added optional `runnable` to `HelperCandidate`, added `runnable` with its doc comment to `DoctorProblemMatch`, returned the ranked runnable with a fallback to `command`, added the `stopped converg` strong cue, added `GENERIC_REPAIR_CUE` and `genericRepairCue`, and updated the module header wording.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts` — imported `genericRepairCue` and added the five requested cases.\n\n**Verify output**\n1. `npx vitest run tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts` (in `ADV`):\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  12 passed (12)\n```\nBaseline before the edit was 8 passed, so the four new test blocks all run green.\n2. `npm run typecheck` (in `ADV`): exit code 0, captured from npm itself.\n3. `rg -c \"stopped converg\" $DH`: `1`.\n\nI also confirmed the two runnable expectations against the real helper script before writing the tests. It ranks `/doctor:agents-md check` and `/doctor:ci report` first for the two prompts, so the assertions pin observed behaviour rather than a guess.\n\n**Not done**\nNothing was left undone. `tasks.md` was not modified and its checkbox is unticked, as instructed.\n\n**Residual risk**\nThe `first.command` fallback in `matchDoctorProblem` has no direct test, because every candidate the helper currently emits carries a `runnable`. The task named only the five cases above, so I did not add a mock-based case for that branch.\n\n**State**\nEdited and uncommitted in the worktree branch `worktrees/352-command-surfacing-research`. Only the two named files were changed by me. Other dirty paths in `git status` belong to other workers.\n\nNext is the orchestrator's move: dispatch wave A2 (`T005`), since wave A1's last task has now printed its expected output.","time":{"start":1794543368729,"end":1794543372794}}}
